.TH "GLESHA-DECRYPT" "1" "" "glesha" "User Commands"
.nh
.ad l
.SH NAME
glesha\-decrypt \- decrypt an archive to a compressed tar file
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBglesha decrypt\fR FILE [options]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Decrypt the archive FILE and write the compressed tar file it contains. The output file must not exist. Use 'glesha extract' to unpack files instead.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-output FILE
Write to FILE (default: NAME.tar.EXT next to the input).
.SS Passphrase options
.TP
.B \-\-passphrase\-file FILE
Read the archive passphrase from FILE ('\-': stdin). A trailing newline is ignored. Without this option, the passphrase is read from a hidden prompt.
.SS Performance options
.TP
.B \-\-memory\-max SIZE
Memory limit (default: half of available memory). SIZE takes a unit such as MiB or GiB and must be at least 48MiB. If available memory cannot be determined, 128MiB is used.
.PP
The global options described in glesha(1) are also accepted.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
glesha decrypt documents.tar.xz.gpg
glesha decrypt documents.tar.xz.gpg \-\-output documents.tar.xz
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR glesha (1),
.BR glesha\-archive (1),
.BR glesha\-extract (1)
